## PenguScript manual declaration binding for rlights.h - the raylib-6 era
## "RLG" lighting framework vendored in std_c/rlights.h.
## rlights: https://github.com/raysan5/raylib/blob/master/examples/shaders/
##          shaders_lightmap.c lineage - this vendored copy is the newer
##          context-based RLG_ API (see header's own comments / LICENSE).
##
## This is a declaration file (.d.pengu): it declares a curated subset of the
## native C surface so the LSP and the semantic checker know how to call
## rlights from PenguScript.
##
## IMPORTANT - why there is no `include "rlights.h"` here: rlights.h pulls in
## raylib.h AND an OpenGL loader header (`GL_HEADER`, default
## "external/glad.h") at the very top of the file, unconditionally. A plain
## PenguScript bundle cannot provide that include path, and rlights only makes
## sense inside a running raylib/OpenGL application. This module is therefore
## a semantic REFERENCE binding: it lets `pengu check`, the LSP and editor
## tooling see the function shapes, and it documents the API, but importing it
## does not emit the C header and no function may be CALLED from pure Pengu
## yet (their raylib struct/pointer arguments are not constructible in
## PenguScript, and no implementation archive is built). Projects that want
## real rlights use raylib C code (or a future raygui/rlights wrapper) with
## their own `#define RLIGHTS_IMPLEMENTATION` translation unit and link
## raylib; the vendored header then resolves `GL_HEADER` from the raylib
## sources.
##
## Bound subset (declared subset expressible with plain numbers, bools, ints
## and the opaque RLG_Context handle):
##   - context ............ RLG_CreateContext / DestroyContext / SetContext /
##                          GetContext (opaque handle)
##   - view position ...... RLG_SetViewPosition(x, y, z)
##   - parallax layers .... RLG_SetParallaxLayers / GetParallaxLayers
##   - light control ...... RLG_UseLight / IsLightUsed / ToggleLight /
##                          SetLightType / GetLightType / SetLightValue /
##                          SetLightXYZ / GetLightValue / LightTranslate /
##                          LightRotateX / LightRotateY / LightRotateZ /
##                          SetLightTarget
##   - shadows ............ RLG_EnableShadow / DisableShadow /
##                          IsShadowEnabled / SetShadowBias / GetShadowBias
##
## INTENTIONALLY OMITTED (documented - why the subset is small):
##   - every signature that passes a raylib struct BY VALUE or BY REF
##     (Vector2/3, Color, Shader, MaterialMap, Material, Mesh, Model,
##     Matrix, Texture, RLG_Skybox, RLG_DrawFunc callbacks, ...). Those
##     types live in std/raylib.d.pengu and mixing the two modules' type
##     namespaces is fragile, so the affected functions
##     (RLG_SetViewPositionV/GetViewPosition, ambient color, light color,
##     RLG_*V vec3 variants, shadow-map updates, mesh/model casting,
##     skybox loading/drawing, map control) are left unbound.
##   - the implementation is NOT compiled into the Pengu runtime (it needs
##     raylib + OpenGL and only has meaning inside a windowed app).
##
## Enum constants (usable directly in comparisons, values from the header):
##   RLG_LightType:      RLG_DIRLIGHT = 0, RLG_OMNILIGHT = 1, RLG_SPOTLIGHT = 2
##   RLG_LightProperty:  RLG_LIGHT_POSITION = 0, RLG_LIGHT_DIRECTION = 1,
##                       RLG_LIGHT_COLOR = 2, RLG_LIGHT_ENERGY = 3,
##                       RLG_LIGHT_SPECULAR = 4, RLG_LIGHT_SIZE = 5,
##                       RLG_LIGHT_INNER_CUTOFF = 6, RLG_LIGHT_OUTER_CUTOFF = 7,
##                       RLG_LIGHT_DISTANCE = 8, RLG_LIGHT_ATTENUATION = 9
##
## Type mapping notes:
##   - RLG_Context is `typedef void* RLG_Context` in the header, declared
##     here as an opaque handle alias.
##   - enum parameters/returns are typed `int`; angles/values are `f32`.

# NOTE: there is deliberately NO `include "rlights.h"` in this file (see the
# module doc comment above: the header pulls in raylib.h plus an OpenGL
# loader, and no rlights implementation archive is built). This binding is a
# semantic/reference module: it documents the API and satisfies `pengu check`
# / LSP, but its functions must not be called from pure PenguScript yet -
# calling them would emit C calls without a prototype or a definition.

# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Types
# ------------------------------------------------------------------

alias RLG_Context as opaque

# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Functions (real C symbol names used verbatim - no insignia)
# ------------------------------------------------------------------

declare RLG_CreateContext into RLG_Context

declare RLG_DestroyContext with ctx as RLG_Context into void

declare RLG_SetContext with ctx as RLG_Context into void

declare RLG_GetContext into RLG_Context

declare RLG_SetViewPosition with x as f32, y as f32, z as f32 into void

declare RLG_SetParallaxLayers with min as int, max as int into void

declare RLG_GetParallaxLayers with min as ref to int, max as ref to int into void

declare RLG_UseLight with light as int, active as bool into void

declare RLG_IsLightUsed with light as int into bool

declare RLG_ToggleLight with light as int into void

declare RLG_SetLightType with light as int, type as int into void

declare RLG_GetLightType with light as int into int

declare RLG_SetLightValue with light as int, property as int, value as f32 into void

declare RLG_SetLightXYZ with light as int, property as int, x as f32, y as f32, z as f32 into void

declare RLG_GetLightValue with light as int, property as int into f32

declare RLG_LightTranslate with light as int, x as f32, y as f32, z as f32 into void

declare RLG_LightRotateX with light as int, degrees as f32 into void

declare RLG_LightRotateY with light as int, degrees as f32 into void

declare RLG_LightRotateZ with light as int, degrees as f32 into void

declare RLG_SetLightTarget with light as int, x as f32, y as f32, z as f32 into void

declare RLG_EnableShadow with light as int, shadowMapResolution as int into void

declare RLG_DisableShadow with light as int into void

declare RLG_IsShadowEnabled with light as int into bool

declare RLG_SetShadowBias with light as int, value as f32 into void

declare RLG_GetShadowBias with light as int into f32
